From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:07:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Enable CSS Scroll Snap's properties behind a pref

scroll-snap-type, scroll-snap-align, scroll-snap-stop, the eight
scroll-padding longhands and the scroll-padding, scroll-padding-block and
scroll-padding-inline shorthands were Gecko's only, so Servo-mode engines
dropped them at parse. They are now on in Servo mode behind
`layout.css.scroll-snap.enabled`, as scroll-behavior and
overscroll-behavior are, for an embedder that snaps scrolls.

ScrollSnapType's and ScrollSnapAlign's fields are public, so that such an
embedder can read a computed value: Gecko reads them through cbindgen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 style/properties/longhands.toml     | 22 +++++++++++-----------
 style/properties/shorthands.toml    |  6 +++---
 style/values/specified/box.rs       | 12 ++++++++----
 stylo_static_prefs/preferences.toml |  1 +
 4 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

